    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The Nearest Centroid classifier within the scikit-learn library was used, and the shrink_threshold parameter was used as the paper's delta hyperparameter. Ten values of delta were evaluated, ranging from 0.01 to 1.0."
      ],
      "id": "e13b5903"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "from sklearn.neighbors import NearestCentroid\n",
        "\n",
        "delta_values = np.linspace(0.01, 1.0, 10)  # 10 evenly spaced values from 0.01 to 1.0\n",
        "model = NearestCentroid(metric='euclidean')"
      ],
      "id": "2d383e42",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The standard 10-fold CV approach was used to determine the optimal delta hyperparameter, delta star. For each value of delta, the mean CV accuracy was determined. The delta star hyperparameter corresponded to the delta value that produced the greatest mean CV accuracy. In other words, the delta star hyperparameter corresponded to the delta value that produced the smallest mean CV error. "
      ],
      "id": "1b0f94aa"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Use 10-fold CV to determine the optimal delta hyperparameter\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import cross_val_score, KFold\n",
        "kf = KFold(n_splits=10, shuffle=True, random_state=1) \n",
        "\n",
        "# Initialize a list to store mean CV scores for each delta value\n",
        "cv_scores = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for delta in delta_values:\n",
        "    model.set_params(shrink_threshold=delta)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    scores = cross_val_score(\n",
        "        model,  # nearest centroid model as defined above\n",
        "        X,      # feature matrix\n",
        "        y,      # labels - Class 1 and Class 2\n",
        "        cv=kf,  # CV using the Kfold as defined above\n",
        "        scoring='accuracy'\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    \n",
        "    cv_scores.append(scores.mean())  # store mean CV score for each delta value\n",
        "\n",
        "idx_max_score = np.argmax(cv_scores)  # returns the index of the delta value that had the highest mean CV score\n",
        "delta_star = delta_values[idx_max_score]  # returns the delta value that had the highest mean CV score\n",
        "cv_error_delta_star = 1 - cv_scores[idx_max_score]  # returns the mean CV error for the optimal delta\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Delta star value: {delta_star}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Mean CV error for delta star: {cv_error_delta_star:.3f}\")"
      ],
      "id": "2627f71f",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "A classifier model, delta star model, was then developed using the optimal delta hyperparameter and trained on the original dataset. The error of this model was estimated on a larger simulated null dataset of 1000 samples. The paper used a dataset of 20,000 samples, but a smaller dataset was used here to reduce computation time. Then the true error of the delta star model was determined by comparing the predicted class labels to the true class labels of the larger null dataset."
      ],
      "id": "68f009c2"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# create delta star model with delta star hyperparameter\n",
        "model_delta_star = NearestCentroid(metric='euclidean', shrink_threshold=delta_star)\n",
        "\n",
        "# fit model on original dataset\n",
        "model_delta_star.fit(X, y)\n",
        "\n",
        "# generate new, null dataset with 1000 samples\n",
        "X_eval, y_eval = generate_noise_data(n_samples=1000, n_features=100)\n",
        "\n",
        "# use model to predict class on the new, larger null dataset\n",
        "y_pred = model_delta_star.predict(X_eval)\n",
        "\n",
        "# determine true error of the delta star model\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score\n",
        "accuracy = accuracy_score(y_eval, y_pred)\n",
        "true_error_delta_star = 1 - accuracy\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"True error estimate for delta star model: {true_error_delta_star:.3f}\")"
      ],
      "id": "eca57074",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
